02:16:22.750 --> 02:16:25.100
So, yes, I want the full experience.

02:16:25.100 --> 02:16:25.940
Show me everything.

02:16:26.299 --> 02:16:27.879
I want it from a particular point of view.

02:16:27.879 --> 02:16:31.049
And I don't want to hear from these other
people who I don't like, by the way.

02:16:31.049 --> 02:16:32.410
It's going to be, my eight
year old is using this.

02:16:32.440 --> 02:16:34.309
I don't want anything that's
going to cause a problem.

02:16:34.309 --> 02:16:37.779
And I want everything filtered and
AI based filters like that that you

02:16:37.780 --> 02:16:41.410
program and control are going to work
much better and be much more honest

02:16:41.410 --> 02:16:43.690
and straightforward and clear and
so forth than what we have today.

02:16:44.469 --> 02:16:46.999
Anyway, basically, what I want people
to do is think, every time you think

02:16:47.000 --> 02:16:49.400
of a risk of how it can be used,
just think of like, okay, we can

02:16:49.400 --> 02:16:50.570
use it to build a countermeasure.

02:16:50.980 --> 02:16:52.720
And the great thing about
the countermeasures is they

02:16:52.720 --> 02:16:55.379
can not only offset AI risks,
they can offset other risks.

02:16:55.450 --> 02:16:55.740
Right?

02:16:55.740 --> 02:16:59.139
Because we already live in a world
where pathogens are a problem, right?

02:16:59.410 --> 02:17:01.239
We ought to have better vaccines anyway.

02:17:01.929 --> 02:17:04.329
We already live in a world where there's
cyber hacking and cyber terrorism.

02:17:04.329 --> 02:17:06.559
They already live in a world where
there's bad content on the Internet.

02:17:06.559 --> 02:17:09.610
And we have the ability now to
build much better AI powered tools

02:17:09.610 --> 02:17:10.590
to deal with all those things.

02:17:12.100 --> 02:17:14.560
Andrew Huberman: I also love
